FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs:2300 — the distribution test claims bucket counts "notice that the lookup is not walking the whole table", but it only inspects buckets maintained at insertion time. If `intern` were reverted to a full `G_INTERN` scan while still calling `intern_bucket_add` on misses, `spread_growth`, `distinct_buckets`, `max_chain` and the ordinary-name checks would all still pass. The phase's central performance property therefore has no guard that can fail for a linear-lookup regression — add a counter of table comparisons (or a timing/work probe) and assert lookups stay near the bucket size, or drop the overclaim.
2. [MINOR] phases/phase-074/REPORT.md:119 — the known-gaps entry still says "The hidden self-test route in `main` works around it with a flag", but that route no longer exists: there is no `--intern-selftest` string in any `.rb` file and `bootstrap/compiler.rb` ends with a plain `main()` (line 3306). The report contradicts its own "main ... untouched" description and the actual tree; remove or rewrite the sentence to describe the `bootstrap/intern_selftest.rb` fragment.

